Phase 1 — Explicit timeout hierarchy

Replace ambiguous timeout behavior with an explicit bounded hierarchy.

The architecture should distinguish at minimum:

- connection/setup timeout;
- provider response/inference timeout;
- individual case deadline;
- whole experiment/run deadline.

Do not allow a hidden outer five-minute context to kill an inner fifteen-minute inference operation.

Likewise, do not allow "http.Client.Timeout" to silently override the intended provider inference deadline.

Prefer context-based cancellation for the overall inference operation.

