## Pass 6.1 report

  ### Root cause

  The ~300-second failures came from Ollama’s
  http.Client.Timeout = 5m, configured before experiment flags
  were parsed. The artifact’s Client.Timeout ... while reading
  body message confirms that client-wide deadline fired.

  A second bug converted the resulting structured-generation
  error into model_output_malformed using string matching for
  “structured”/“JSON”.

  ### Corrections

  - Added typed failure codes:
      - PROVIDER_CONNECTION_ERROR
      - PROVIDER_TIMEOUT
      - PROVIDER_CANCELLED
      - PROVIDER_RESPONSE_ERROR
      - MODEL_OUTPUT_MALFORMED
      - VERIFICATION_ERROR
      - EXECUTION_ERROR

  - Removed the Ollama whole-request HTTP timeout.
  - Transport timeout now protects connection/TLS setup.
  - Context deadlines control inference, case, and run
    execution.

  - Defaults are configurable through:
      - --inference-timeout (15m)
      - --case-timeout
      - --run-timeout

  - Runtime policy is persisted in RunConfig and therefore
    included in ConfigurationHash.

  - Added --case-id memory-001.
  - Added worst-case execution-envelope reporting and warnings.

  ### Instrumentation

  Each provider call now records:

  - attempted, completed, failed, timed-out, and successful-
    response counts;

  - start and finish timestamps;
  - request initiation;
  - headers/stream opening;
  - first content;
  - stream progress/chunks/completion;
  - timeout/cancellation;
  - provider duration;
  - prompt/completion tokens when reported;
  - partial response telemetry on failure.

  ModelCalls retains successful-response semantics.
  ProviderAccounting.Attempted distinguishes an unattempted
  request from a timed-out request.

  Duration fields now separate provider, retrieval, graph/
  search, verification, orchestration, and total attempt time.

  ### Memory integrity

  The hash changes were caused by unconditional episodic
  learning after BAN execution, including provider failures with
  no measurement.

  Episode writes now require a measured non-error outcome and
  produce an explicit APPEND_EPISODE mutation event. Provider
  failures leave both useful-memory and misleading-memory stores
  unchanged. Each condition now reports its own actual initial/
  final hashes.

  ### Graph audit

  NodesCreated:0 / DuplicatesDetected:5 was a metrics bug, not
  evidence of five duplicate evaluations:

  - failed traces populated nodes only at successful
    finalization;

  - duplicate count was inferred as configured proposals minus
    recorded nodes.

  Failure traces now finalize graph state, and duplicates are
  counted only from actual fingerprint collisions. Metrics
  distinguish candidate proposals, accepted nodes, duplicate
  proposals, provider evaluations, and pruned candidates.

  ### Outcome semantics

  Execution failures remain unmeasured failures and are excluded
  from reasoning comparisons. Failed conditions cannot be
  classified as helpful or harmful memory effects. Pairwise
  memory comparisons skip execution-failed observations.

